# Migration launch collaboration

Rotate business, engineering/operations and UAT roles. Compare normalized content, preserve post-cutover changes and document rollback boundaries.

## Input and contract
input/fixture.json; input/dictionary.md; project version 1

## Finding and reproducible output
```json
{
  "reconciliation": {
    "normalized": [
      {
        "id": "U1",
        "email": "alice@example.invalid",
        "status": "active"
      },
      {
        "id": "U2",
        "email": "bob@example.invalid",
        "status": "pending"
      }
    ],
    "differences": [
      "U2"
    ],
    "rollbackAllowed": false,
    "preserve": [
      "U3"
    ]
  },
  "decision": "preserve_delta_before_rollback",
  "feedback": {
    "to": "ops",
    "issue": "new_data_preservation"
  },
  "revision": 2
}
```

## Failure prevented
A rollback that discards the new records must be blocked.

## Decision and limits
Accept only the specified result set. Escalate a missing identity, permission, business probe or required not-run item. This is an original synthetic teaching reference, not evidence of learner execution or real employment.

## Contribution and handoff
Reference authored with AI assistance for Avemly. The learner must replace this attribution with their own factual contribution; review open criteria before archiving.

